course: dictionary
lesson: 14419
title: Overpower: when strength takes over
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To overpower means to beat someone by being stronger, so they cannot fight back. «The guards overpowered the thief at the castle gate.» The thief was stronger than nobody here, so the guards must have been stronger. Look for clue words like strong, held down or could not fight back.
explain: The word can also describe a smell or a taste. «The smell of garlic overpowered the soup, so we could not taste the carrots.» The garlic was so strong that it took over. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "The garlic took over the soup" makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The adjective overpowering means too strong. «The smell of old socks was overpowering.» Nobody wants to be near it. If something is so strong you cannot bear it, it is overpowering.
fact: Overpower is a verb: overpower, overpowers, overpowered, overpowering.
fact: «Overpower» means to beat someone by being stronger, so they cannot fight back.
fact: «Overpowered» can describe a smell, taste or feeling that is so strong it takes over.
fact: «Overpowering» means too strong, as in an overpowering smell.
fact: In games, «OP» is slang for overpowered: a character or item that is too strong to be fair.
exercise: «The guards overpowered the thief at the castle gate.» What does overpowered mean? | Woke him up gently | Chased him around the castle | *Beat him by being stronger, so he could not fight back | Gave him a present
exercise: «The smell of garlic overpowered the soup.» What does overpowered suggest? | The soup was thrown away | *The garlic smell was so strong it took over | The garlic was mild and gentle | The soup was cold
exercise: Lena says overpowering means very weak. What is the right meaning? | Very weak and quiet | *Too strong to bear | Very long | Very kind and friendly
test: In a game, someone says a character is OP. What does OP mean? | *Too strong to be fair | Lost somewhere in the game | Made of paper | Very slow and sleepy
test: Which sentence uses overpower to mean beat someone by being stronger? | The wrestler bought a new hat for the match. | The wrestler sang loudly at the party. | *The wrestler overpowered his rival and pinned him down. | The wrestler slept on the bus.
exam: Which word in «The loud music overpowered the quiet birds» is the verb that means took over? | loud | birds | *overpowered | music
